1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:02,870
Not sure which title or thumbnail to use? 

2
00:00:02,870 --> 00:00:08,160
Try “A/B\h\htesting,”  a feature that lets you\h
choose up to 3 video titles and/or\h\h

3
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:12,640
thumbnails to test with viewers to help\h
pick your winner. Here’s how it works.

4
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:17,600
Eligible creators can use the “A/B testing”\h
feature through YouTube Studio desktop\h\h

5
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:22,640
when publishing a new video, or with an\h
existing video. On the Video Details page,\h\h

6
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:26,720
click the icon under the ‘Title’ section\h
or ‘Thumbnail section. From here,\h\h

7
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:31,040
choose if you want to run a Title\h
only test, a Thumbnail only test,\h\h

8
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:35,280
or a Title and Thumbnail test.
For title only, you can add up\h\h

9
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:39,920
to three different titles to test.\h
Titles must be under 100 characters.\h

10
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:44,320
For thumbnail only, you can upload three\h
different images to learn which viewers\h\h

11
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:50,000
prefer. For title and thumbnail, you can add\h
three different title and thumbnail combinations

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,920
After you’ve added your titles, thumbnails or\h
combinations of both, click Done. A/B testing is\h\h

13
00:00:55,920 --> 00:01:01,440
only available for Public, long form videos, and\h
the test will start once you publish your video.

14
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:02,960
Here’s how the test works:\h

15
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:08,320
YouTube will show your chosen titles and/or\h
thumbnails evenly across your video’s audience,\h\h

16
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:13,520
and will select a winning thumbnail based on\h
which one generates the most watch time share\h

17
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:17,840
You can check the status of your test at\h
any time by going to the Video Details\h\h

18
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:22,320
page and clicking “View test report”\h
under the Title or Thumbnail section\h

19
00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:26,080
You’ll see how much time is left for the\h
test and how they’re performing. You can\h\h

20
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:30,480
also choose to stop the test and manually\h
set one of the options as the winner\h

21
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:35,200
If you let the test run, the results\h
may take a few hours or up to a couple\h\h

22
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:37,920
of weeks to be finalized.
How long it takes to get\h\h

23
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:43,040
the results is affected by factors like:
How similar your titles and/or thumbnails\h\h

24
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:46,160
are (the more they differ, the\h
faster your test will finish)\h

25
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:49,840
And your video traffic (the more\h
impressions that your video receives,\h\h

26
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:52,720
the faster your test will finish)
Once the test is finished,\h\h

27
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:57,040
the test report will show the results
If there’s a statistically significant result,\h\h

28
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:01,840
you’ll see a “Winner” label. YouTube will\h
automatically update your video title and/or\h\h

29
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:06,400
thumbnail to this winner when the test is done.
You might also see a “Performed Same” label.\h\h

30
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:11,600
This result indicates that all test options had\h
similar watch time performance. If there’s no\h\h

31
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:15,680
clear winner, or if the options “Performed\h
Same,” the first title and/or thumbnail\h\h

32
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:20,320
will be selected and shown to your audience.
Remember that in either case, it’s ultimately\h\h

33
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:24,880
up to you – you can always manually select\h
the video title and thumbnail you want to use.\h

34
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:29,600
You can also choose to run a new test, but\h
note it will delete your old experiment

35
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:33,120
Now let’s walk through some things\h
to note and best practices for\h\h

36
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:36,880
using the “A/B testing” feature:
Titles and Thumbnails must follow\h\h

37
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:41,520
our Community Guidelines, and the tool will\h
not work on videos that are designated as\h\h

38
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:47,040
made for kids, for mature audiences, or live.
Note that great titles and thumbnails serve\h\h

39
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:52,000
an important purpose beyond getting viewers to\h
click. They help a viewer understand what the\h\h

40
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,160
video is about so that they don't waste\h
their time clicking on the wrong videos.\h

41
00:02:56,160 --> 00:03:01,040
Remember that your title and thumbnail should\h
work together as a team. We highly encourage\h\h

42
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:05,600
testing title and thumbnail combinations\h
to find which pairing works best to help\h\h

43
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:10,720
viewers understand what your video is about.
We suggest testing titles and thumbnails on\h\h

44
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:15,360
a limited selection of older videos for\h
initial guidance, then a selection of more\h\h

45
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:19,680
recent videos you think will provide the most\h
meaningful insights for your content strategy.\h

46
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:23,360
We also recommend testing thumbnail\h
variations that explore different\h\h

47
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:28,880
layout compositions and changes to thumbnail\h
elements (including background, text overlays, and\h\h

48
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:34,160
object placement) to learn which resonates most\h
with your audience. Some tips to keep in mind:\h

49
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:39,520
Ensure your images are balanced, with a focal\h
point to direct viewers attention towards\h

50
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:43,520
Utilize high contrast, allowing\h
your subject to stand out against\h\h

51
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:49,200
the background in both light and dark mode.
With text, remember that fewer words can be\h\h

52
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:53,600
impactful, while too much text can be\h
difficult to process while scrolling.\h

53
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:58,880
And finally when it comes to depth of field, keep\h
your background in mind and play with blank space

54
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:03,360
We hope the A/B testing feature will help you\h
gain insights when it comes to making titles\h\h

55
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:07,760
and thumbnails, and help your overall video\h
performance in the long run! For more info,\h\h

56
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:10,880
check out the links below. Thanks for watching!

